@appointment garden-bed
// SW2, 0.92.6 item 9 (the user: yes). A bed of your own: Tove Cruz (they/them) gives you one small bed in the garden.
// You plant it together (the first scene), then Cruz books three short visits over the next weeks to tend it (one
// line each, `== tend` in order), then the harvest: you pick it and take it to Brennan, and it's in that night's
// dinner (`== harvest`). Your bed gets a little sign. FX22: the crop is lettuce by default (a "week-N lettuce").
title: A bed of your own
starts: invite
host: cruz-tove
gate: tier>=friend !mem:appt.garden-bed
when: Saturday morning, then three short visits about a week apart, then the harvest
at: 10:00-10:30 (the planting); 10 minutes (each visit)
where: 3 room Hydroponics garden: garden
who: host, you
once: yes
mem: appt.garden-bed
flag: garden.bed.planted
record: Grew your own bed of lettuce in the garden.

== invite
- I've got a spare bed. Small. By the tree. Would you... it could be yours. Saturday?
- There's a bed in the garden with nothing in it. It's sad. You could fix that. Saturday?

== busy
- Oh. Not this Saturday? Next one, then. The bed will wait. Beds are patient.

== mail
- Saturday, {time}: Cruz is giving you a bed in the garden. Wear old clothes. Soil gets everywhere.

== scene
cruz-tove: This one. By the tree. It gets the good light in the afternoon. It's yours now.   [gesture]
cruz-tove: Seeds in a line. A finger deep. Not two fingers. One. Then cover them up and say hello.
cruz-tove: That makes it a week-one lettuce. Today's its birthday.   [nod]
? choice
* Say hello to the seeds.   flavour:cheer mem:appt.garden-bed
  cruz-tove: They heard you. I always know when they hear.   [laugh]
* Ask what to call the bed.   flavour:share mem:appt.garden-bed
  cruz-tove: I'll make a sign. Your name on it. Small letters. Plants are shy.   [nod]
cruz-tove: I'll come and find you next week. We'll check on it. Ten minutes. It's enough.

== tend
cruz-tove: Look. Shoots. Week two. Tiny. Don't touch them, just look. Lovely.
cruz-tove: Week three. Water at the roots. You remembered. They're leaning to the light. Good sign.
cruz-tove: Week four. Nearly. One more week and Brennan will be after them. We'll beat her to it.

== harvest
cruz-tove: Today. Pick from the outside in. Leave the heart, it grows back. There. That's yours.   [gesture]
cruz-tove: Take it to Brennan. She'll put it in tonight's salad, and she'll say whose.
cruz-tove: Your first crop. I'll put a little mark on the sign. Week five. A good week.   [nod]

== thanks
- Cruz gives you a bed of your own in the garden, by the tree, with your name on a little sign.   #warm

== after
- Your lettuce was in the salad tonight. Brennan told the whole mess whose it was.   #warm
- Your bed's doing well. Cruz checks it every morning. Don't tell them I said.   #warm
